    "beat": 1,
    "flux": "At first light, a weathered lighthouse keeper stands on a black granite jetty, holding a tangle of rope and net. In the center of the frame, a small translucent fish glows pale aqua inside the mesh, illuminating her mud-stained gloves and face. Composition: low angle, keeper left, glowing fish slightly right of center, sea spray foreground. Lens: 35 mm, shallow depth. Light: cool dawn blue, soft mist, faint warm rim from sunrise. Palette: slate blue, charcoal, pale cyan, ivory, rust orange. Style: cinematic realism, high detail, atmospheric, quiet, painterly realism.",
    "ltx": "Silent dawn on a rocky shore. The keeper's hand pulls the net upward; wet rope twists and glistens. Inside the net, the glowing fish flexes its tail, sending ripples of cyan light through water and fibers. Her head tilts, breath fogs, then a soft exhale. Camera: slow push-in from wide medium to close-up on the fish, slight handheld wobble, ending on the glow. Pacing: slow, quiet, continuous, no music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 2,
    "flux": "Interior spiral staircase inside a lighthouse at dusk, a keeper climbs with a bucket containing the glowing fish. Composition: circular staircase dominates frame, keeper ascending right to left, fish light pooling at lower left. Lens: 50 mm, slightly low angle. Light: storm-darkness, cold blue window slits, warm cyan fish glow, flickering shadows. Palette: deep navy, charcoal, silver, turquoise, amber highlights. Style: moody cinematic realism, wet textures, rain-streaked glass, tense, detailed, dramatic chiaroscuro.",
    "ltx": "Silent stormy climb. The keeper rises step by step on the spiral stair, boots gripping metal treads. Rain strikes small windows; gusts shake the lantern light. The fish pulses in the bucket, throwing moving cyan reflections across stone, rope, and her coat. Camera: tracking shot following her from behind, then rotating slightly to reveal the circular stair and worsening storm outside. Pacing: steady, accelerating slightly, continuous, no music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 3,
    "flux": "Lighthouse lamp room at night, a large brass Fresnel lens centered high. Below, the keeper sets the bucket near the lantern; the glowing fish expands the light into brilliant gold. Composition: symmetrical, lens vertical axis, keeper lower third left, fish glow bursting upward. Lens: 24 mm wide interior. Light: intense golden radiance, white-hot core, cyan remnants, sharp flares through prismatic glass. Palette: gold, amber, ivory, deep navy, brass. Style: cinematic fantasy realism, radiant, awe, crisp mechanical detail, luminous particles, dramatic contrast.",
    "ltx": "Silent transformation in the lamp room. The keeper places the bucket on the platform; the fish thrashes once, and its light surges upward through the lantern. Gold illumination expands through the Fresnel lens, turning every glass facet into a bright prism. Reflections run across metal grates, the keeper's face, and her hands. Camera: slow tilt up from bucket to lamp, then a gentle dolly-out as the room floods with gold. Pacing: quiet, building, then sudden luminous release, no music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 4,
    "flux": "Stormy sea at night, a small fishing ship approaches jagged black rocks beneath a towering lighthouse. The lighthouse beam is a sweeping golden searchlight cutting through rain, guiding the ship past the hazards. Composition: ship lower left, rocks lower right, lighthouse high left, gold beam diagonal across frame. Lens: 35 mm, low sea-level angle. Light: storm blue, white spray, dominant warm gold beam, wet highlights. Palette: black, indigo, silver, gold, pale white. Style: cinematic epic realism, dramatic weather, dynamic motion blur, high contrast, hopeful.",
    "ltx": "Silent rescue at sea. The ship turns, hull heaving through choppy water, waves breaking over black rocks. Rain falls in sheets; spray flies. The gold beam sweeps across the water, illuminating the ship's bow and guiding it around the rocks. The keeper's hand appears at the lamp room railing, steadying the light. Camera: wide tracking shot from the water, panning with the ship, then pulling up to reveal the lighthouse beam. Pacing: urgent, continuous, steady, no music, no speech."
  }
